---
import Book from '../layouts/Book.astro';import{lessons,definitions,label,moduleNames}from'../lib/content';
---
<Book title="Prerequisite map"><span class="eyebrow">THE ACTUAL CURRICULUM GRAPH</span><h1>Prerequisite map</h1><p class="dek">This table is generated from the same manifest as the sidebar. Each row points to earlier concepts; the build rejects missing references and cycles.</p><div class="context-box"><p>Deutsch and Grover are independent starting points. Module00 is an on-demand library, never a prerequisite lock. A lesson's numbered position is a suggested route; dependency links state what its explanation reuses.</p></div>{moduleNames.slice(1).map((name,i)=><section><h2>{name}</h2><ul class="catalog-list">{lessons.filter(l=>l.module===i+1).map(l=><li><a href={`/lessons/${l.id}/`}>{label(l)}</a><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> {l.prerequisites.length?l.prerequisites.map((id,j)=><Fragment>{j>0?' · ':''}<a style="font-size:12px" href={`/lessons/${id}/`}>{lessons.find(x=>x.id===id)?.title??id}</a></Fragment>):'No earlier lesson required.'}</p><p><strong>Mathematics introduced or reused:</strong> {[...new Set([...l.concepts,...l.reusedConcepts])].map((id,j)=><Fragment>{j>0?' · ':''}<a style="font-size:12px" href={`/definitions/${id}/`}>{definitions.find(d=>d.id===id)?.title??id}</a></Fragment>)}</p></li>)}</ul></section>)}<p><a href="/curriculum.json">Download the machine-readable manifest</a></p></Book>
